

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 6

                                  FOR

                                AGESILAO







          Fabrizio Zordan
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Agesilao has been informed by Babba Sissoko (#0) that his 
cooperation has become expendable, and therefore our previously amicable 
relations are now broken.

  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Kwoth (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Agesilao 
treated with his ally Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally 
Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Agesilao treated with his ally Circe (#8).
  With the coming of the spring season, Agesilao set out to quench his 
thirst for glory.  He moved into Black Forest (#1808) with his high-spirited 
army.  He was informed by some peasants of a perilous feature in Black 
Forest previously unknown to us, a Monastery (#58) inhabited by 
the Renegade Illusionist.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The 
mysterious Renegade Illusionist is said to be a shadowy figure who uses his 
powers of deception to preserve his solitary existence.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  Agesilao announced a call 
for recruits in Black Forest and was able to form the 34th Trolls to fight 
for Agesilao.
  In late summer, Agesilao practiced his Druidism diligently for months, but 
could make no progress.
  With the coming of the fall season, Agesilao practiced his Druidism well, 
and even consulted a palm reader, but could not improve his skill in 
Druidism.

  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest in the Christmas Sea, a Sea province owing its allegiance to 
Agesilao.  Lakes (#64)'s forces conquered the Christmas Sea without any 
major engagements.  Lakes leads approximately 1 Bowmen and 1 Fleet.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Agesilao marched on Mare Frigidis 
(#1708) with his formidable forces.

    Agesilao was visited by a hero from Valhalla, named Nixie!    Speaketh  
Nixie: "Hmm.    .    .     Excuse me, are you in need of help?    Druids can 
be quite useful.    It's amazing how those dragons and eagles and ents and 
whales  and so on respond.    (-Emperor and Admiral,David Ruzic, Game 137, 
Jan 1993).    The characteristics for this great King from Game 137 are 
given in your  "CHARACTERS" report.
  If Nixie searches a feature, any monetary treasure Nixie captures will be 
given to you.  If Nixie captures a magic treasure, Nixie will give it to 
your King when he departs for Valhalla, or you can order Nixie to Give it to 
one of your characters.  You can do anything you want with the magic item 
Nixie came with, but the item will leave at the end of her stay with you.  
Except for the rules given in this paragraph, Nixie can generally be treated 
just like your other Heroes, and can be affected by any spell except 
Resurrection.  The main limitation in using Nixie is that Nixie has only 
enough patience to practice with you for one of the phase(s) Nixie is with 
you.  Nixie will leave at the end of the last phase Nixie is scheduled to 
serve you, after all battles have been fought.  Nixie can lead armies, but 
when Nixie returns to Valhalla, the armies will normally be left leaderless 
in the province they are in.  If Nixie has the armies in a province you 
don't own, they will be transferred to your lowest-numbered leader in the 
same province, or at last resort, the garrison commander in an adjacent 
province owned by you.  If no leader is available, the armies will be 
disbanded.
  Nixie can be given orders only for the first 4 phase(s) of the turn.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Agesilao for this year.


  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Kwoth (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Agesilao 
treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Agesilao treated with his ally Kahn 
(#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Agesilao 
treated with his ally Circe (#8).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Jolin (#37) grew tired of the scenery in Apurimac and left for Big Sky.
  Astelle (#82) arose one morning with a desire to see the First Sea, and so 
left Black Forest to journey to that province.


  Here is the financial report for Agesilao's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 51 gold in revenue.  3 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 34th Trolls and the 161st Eagles trained well and improved in 
quality.  47 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Agesilao was left 
with 29 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Moosu, Squire to Tancred
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Tancred announced a call for volunteers in the First Sea and 
was able to enlist the 161st Eagles to fight for Tancred.
  With the coming of the early summer season Tancred moved into Black Forest 
(#1808) with his redoubtable army.
  Midsummer's day passed and a pleasant late summer came.  Tancred was 
instructed in Druidism by Agesilao.  Tancred practiced well and improved his 
skill in Druidism.
  In fall, Tancred practiced hard for months and his skill in Druidism 
increased.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Astelle rebuffed Tancred's 
offer of employment, ridiculing Agesilao's alignment and saying "That 
Agesilao is the most tyrannical ruler in the world!"  After talking to 
Astelle, Tancred judged her (a Human famous for Thievery) to have an Evil, 
Cowardly nature.

  Thy humble servant,   Moosu, Squire to Tancred


From: Montgomery, Squire to Negumba
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to spring.  Negumba boldly marched his forces into Mare 
Frigidis (#1708).
  In early summer, Negumba directed the 36th Garrison to remain in Mare 
Frigidis with the provincial garrison commander.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Negumba announced a call for 
recruits in Mare Frigidis and was able to enlist the 125th Phalanx, the 
134th Warg Riders and the 136th Warg Riders to fight for Negumba.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  Negumba marched on Bizerte (#1807) with 
his formidable forces.
  During early winter, Negumba moved into Apurimac (#1806) with his army.  
Northeast of here lies the province of Bam Yanga (#105), ruled by 
Giovanna d'Arco.  It is known to be a Desert province occupied by Humans.  
Their Human warriors fight in the style of Camel Corps.

  Agesilao's minions initiated a campaign of conquest directed at Apurimac, 
a Desert province owing allegiance to Jolin (#37).  Negumba was in command 
of the attacking armies.  The defending forces were led by Jolin.  The 
armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Apurimac (1806):

  136th   
  Wargs   
